const mkTests = () => done('tests') || agent(`${RULES}\nRole: test writer (Engineer), rules.md section (d), for P2 of ${SPEC}. Branch push/vg-p2r-tests, suffix vg-p2r-tests, from origin/main (P1 is on it). Write ONLY ${TEST_FILES} (both new, rewritten for rev 6); never a source file. Do not read, copy or merge anything from ${FIN_REF}, push/vg-p2-tests or push/vg-p2-rulings: the rev 4a tests there are superseded and are rewritten, not edited (spec :136). Header docstring of each file: the rule words word for word (method rev 3): bible E-17 R-193-01 (docs/bible/epics/E-17-map-generation.md:315, "the growth front is ragged from its first ring and a town is never a square or an octagon at any age" is the sentence this proves; paste the whole rule) and R-193-09 (:323, streets along contour lines and rivers; paste), plus the spec sentences they implement (spec ${SPECFILE} :113-137, quoted: "the field's spread is also multiplied by seeded noise ... so the growth front is ragged from its first ring" as spec :115 carries it, the hop-cost and gate sentences, and the DRAFT-shape-harm sentence of :136). The bible gives no number for the cost buckets, the lattice, the window, the share or the pin: say so in the header and cite each as "spec rev 6, DRAFT-<name>". A test whose behaviour none of these or a gap ruling states is not written; report the gap. ${RULE_PINS}\nEvery assertion that proves R-193-01 (the first-ring spread, the front shape, the lots shape, the seeds-differ test and the noise-off control) carries the rule's words in its message, in the form (spec :136): assert <expr>, "${R193}; age %d seed %d share %.3f" % (age, seed, share); an assertion with no age, seed or share of its own uses the same sentence with the numbers it has.\n${IFACE}\n${RULED}\nHOW THE TESTS BUILD (the pattern of tests/csim/test_PP_grid_margin_exact.py:34-59): compile into a temp dir with cc -shared using exactly its FLAGS list (determinism flags, -std=c11 -fPIC -O2 ...), -I csrc, no world: library A = csrc/terrain_noise.c + csrc/economy_field_noise.c + P1's tests/csim/layout_stub_terrain.c (no layout_terrain.c and no temp file: gap 1 ruling); library B = A + csrc/growth_probe.c. The patched builds (divergence, noise-off) copy csrc (ignoring pipe) as the PP test does and compile every csrc/*.c of the copy with -lm. Every cc call asserts res.returncode == 0 with res.stderr[-3000:] as the message. ctypes only; no Python callbacks (stubs are C: use P1's om_stub_terrain kinds 0 flat, 1 lake and cliff where they fit, and write the other stubs as C source strings into the temp dir: a ramp (height = a fixed slope times x, contour lines along gx), a steep ramp (150 wu per 100 wu cell in x, one contour interval per cell at level 0), a constant-height stub, each filling the same om_layout_terrain struct through a ctypes Structure mirror). Pure Python (math) for the spectrum; numpy only if importable in the venv. Test names carry a group prefix so builders can run a group with -k: test_noise_*, test_lane_*, test_field_*, test_shape_*, and controls test_ctrl_noise_*, test_ctrl_lane_*, test_ctrl_field_*, test_ctrl_shape_*; ${T_LANES} holds the noise and lane groups, ${T_PROBE} holds the field and shape groups. The field and shape tests run seeds 1..10 (spec :235: 10 seeds for the death-step and shape tests; the first-ring and front tests take the same seeds), side 240, one core at cell (120, 120) (index 120 * 240 + 120) unless a case says otherwise; every call of om_growth_probe_run passes lot_cap = PROBE_LOT_CAP 8192 as its tenth argument (GAP 2 ruling), except the bad-argument and cap cases.\nPOSITIVE CONTROL FIRST, green today (P1 is on main), in ${T_LANES}: test_ctrl_p1_stub_builds: terrain_noise.c + the stub (without economy_field_noise.c) compile and link, om_stub_terrain(0, &t) fills the struct and t.height_at returns a number: so red below means the P2 files are missing and not that the harness is broken.\nCASES (numbers from the spec, DRAFT names cited; none invented; each test prints its measured value BEFORE it asserts, spec :246). NOISE (spec :136): test_noise_cost_values: om_field_hop_cost over the 10,000 cells of the gap 5 ruling for each of the seeds 1..64 returns only 1, 2 or 3; test_noise_cost_shares: pooled over the sweep each cost holds between 15 and 55 percent of the cells (DRAFT-field-cost-share), the test PRINTS the shares ('FIELD_COST_SHARE cost1=<> cost2=<> cost3=<>', plus the per-seed minimum and maximum share of each cost); test_noise_deterministic: same seed same value, two seeds differ somewhere; test_noise_apply_cost (GAP 12 ruling): om_field_apply_cost(v, f, c) equals the Python float product ((v * f) * f) * f with c multiplications, left to right, bit for bit, for c = 1, 2, 3 and a sample of (v, f) pairs (f in the range of the field's factors, 0.97 to 0.99), and for c = 1 equals v * f; the control is the Python product in the other order (v * (f * f * f)), which differs from the helper for at least one sample pair, so the detector can tell the orders apart; test_noise_pinned_range: om_field_noise_range gives lo, hi with lo <= measured_min and measured_max <= hi (measured by the test through om_tn_fbm2 at seed + 420, 3 octaves, gain 32768, on the same cells), each pin within DRAFT-noise-range-slack 0 to 0.05 of the measured span of its measured extreme; the test PRINTS the measured extremes and the pins ('NOISE_RANGE measured_min=<> measured_max=<> lo=<> hi=<>') so the builder can pin from them. LANES (om_lane_build, as rev 4a, spec :136): test_lane_flat_stub_fallback_only: on the flat stub (constant height, no water) no cell is a contour or water lane cell, every lane cell is a fallback cell of the warped period grid, and the flat stub's core levels reach 1 (the period-4 grid is 44 percent lane: above the 30 percent cap); test_lane_ramp_follows_contours: on the ramp stub, lane cells exist along the contour lines (cells whose floor(h / (150 * 2^L)) differs from the east or south neighbour are lane cells, computed by an independent Python model in the test), and the control test_ctrl_lane_constant_height_zero_contour counts zero contour lane cells on the constant-height stub and more than zero on the ramp (the counter works); test_lane_lake_shore_ring: on the lake stub (P1 kind 1) every non-water cell with a water neighbour among its eight is a lane cell; test_lane_cap: for every core window (41 x 41, clipped) the lane share of non-water cells is at most 30 percent or the core is at level 3, the flat stub reaches level 1, and the control test_ctrl_lane_steep_ramp: on the steep ramp more than 30 percent of a window is lane at level 0 (so the share detector FAILS there) and the cap test passes only because the level rises (report the level you see); test_lane_ties_to_lower_core: cells equally near two cores take the level of the lower core index (asserted; document in the docstring that reordering the core list can change those cells); test_lane_deterministic: same inputs byte-equal output, and the same bytes at -O0 and -O2 builds. FIELD (library B; spec :136 'probe, field'): test_field_ring_bound: one centred core, age 150: the maximum P over Chebyshev ring k is at most 0.99^k for k in 1..20; test_field_first_ring: age 10 (the core gets exactly its age in growth steps, so age 10 is the field after 10 growth steps): the eight compass-ray reaches (N, S, E, W, NE, NW, SE, SW: the largest distance in cells along the ray with P > 0) are not all equal and the largest exceeds the smallest by at least DRAFT-first-ring-spread 2 cells; print 'FIELD_FIRST_RING seed=<s> reaches=<list> spread=<n>'; test_field_front_shape: for ages 3, 5, 10 and 20 the reached set (cells with P > 0) has a 32-sector radial profile (r(theta) = the largest distance in cells from the core cell of any reached cell in each of DRAFT-shape-sectors 32 sectors, an empty sector 0) whose harmonic 4 plus 8 share (below) is under DRAFT-shape-harm 0.5; print 'FIELD_FRONT steps=<n> seed=<s> harm=<x> pin=0.5' BEFORE the assertion; test_field_death_step (GAP 4 ruling): age 150: out_death_step is above DRAFT-death-floor 100 and below DRAFT-death-steps 600; print 'PROBE_DEATH seed=<s> death=<d> east=<r>' (r the largest gx - 120 with P > 0 at gy = 120), and assert r < 119 (GAP 4 ruling: the field never touches the border of the 240 box, so the shape test is unclipped; r is printed); a measured death step outside the bounds, or r >= 119, is not a test defect: STOP with stop_reason 'death-step-outside: <numbers>' or 'front-touches-border: <numbers>' (spec :136 and the GAP 4 ruling); test_field_deterministic: same inputs byte-equal (P, density, lot_core, death step) and the same bytes at -O0 and -O2; test_field_bad_arguments: -1 for NULL core_cells, NULL ages, n_cores 0 and 7, side 0 and 241, an age of -1 and 401, a core cell at side*side (and the cap cases of the GAP 2 ruling: at age 40 lot_cap 100 gives at most 100 lots, lot_cap 0 and -5 give the same bytes as lot_cap 8192); test_field_lot_counts_printed: seed 1, side 240, core (120, 120), ages 10 and 40: print 'PROBE_LOTS age=<a> lots=<n> eligible=<e>' (e = the number of cells with out_density >= 0.10; the spec expects about 150 and about 600) and assert lots == min(15 * age, floor(0.6 * e)) (the quota of spec :134 for a single core, exact because the field of a core of age at most 40 reaches at most 40 cells and lies inside the 97 x 97 scan square, and the cap term (the lot_cap passed, 8192) is at least 600; say so in the docstring). SHAPE (spec :136 'probe, shape'): test_shape_harmonic_share: for each core age in 10, 20, 30, 40, 100, 200 and seeds 1..10: the radial profile r(theta) of the town's lots = the largest distance in cells from the core cell of any lot in each of 32 sectors (sector = floor(atan2(dy, dx) / (2 pi / 32)) mod 32; an empty sector is 0); the one-sided AC power spectrum of the 32 samples (mean removed, DFT, harmonics 1 to 16); share = (power of harmonics 4 and 8) / (power of harmonics 1 to 16), 0.0 when the total AC power is 0; assert share < DRAFT-shape-harm 0.5; PRINT one line per (age, seed): 'PROBE_SHAPE age=<a> seed=<s> harm=<x> pin=0.5 lots=<n> death=<d>' BEFORE the assertion so the numbers exist even when it fails; also print the 90 degree and 45 degree rotation correlations of r(theta) ('PROBE_ROT ...', printed, not asserted; DRAFT-shape-corr 0.6 is a print label only); test_shape_seeds_differ (GAP 11 ruling = TD-VG-P-1, scope-narrowed): for each age, seeds s and s+1 (1..10) give lot sets whose symmetric difference is at least DRAFT-seed-differ 10 percent of their union, ASSERTED for ages 20, 30, 40, 100 and 200 only; age 10 prints its ratios and asserts nothing; the threshold 0.10 is untouched; print 'PROBE_DIFFER age=<a> seeds=<s>,<s+1> ratio=<r>' for every pair at every age BEFORE asserting (the age-10 lines marked 'reported only'). CONTROLS: test_ctrl_shape_detector_flags_known_bad and test_ctrl_shape_detector_passes_blob: lot sets built in the test (cells of a side 240 grid about (120, 120), radius about 20 cells) are flagged (share above 0.5) for a clean square, a noisy square (sector noise 0.1 of the radius), an octagon and a diamond, and a noise-warped blob (a smooth low-harmonic radius modulation, NOT a 4-lobed shape: lanes are not lobes) passes (share below 0.5); the spec reports measured values square 0.99, diamond 0.99, octagon 0.997, noisy square 0.80, noise blobs 0.13 to 0.20 and says a rasterised disc (0.48 to 0.84) is NOT a control: print your values beside those; if a control does not behave (a bad shape not above 0.5, or the blob not below), STOP with stop_reason 'control-mismatch: <numbers>' (report, do not retune the controls). NOISE OFF (test_ctrl_field_noise_off, spec :136): a build of a patched COPY of csrc in a temp dir (shutil.copytree ignoring pipe, as the PP test does) where growth_probe.c's one line '#define PROBE_HOP_COST(seed, gx, gy) ...' has its right-hand side replaced by 1 (regex on that line; assert exactly one match, as the PP test does): on it the reached set after 10 steps (core age 10) is the Chebyshev square (all eight compass reaches equal 10, harmonic share above 0.9) and the first-ring detector of test_field_first_ring FAILS; on the real build the same detector passes. DIVERGENCE (test_ctrl_field_divergence_patched_build_fails, GAP 3 ruling): the patched copy where PROBE_BASE_DECAY and PROBE_NONWATER_FAR are both 1.01 fails the ring bound (P at ring k <= 0.99^k) and the death-step test (age 400, out_death_step == -1); on the real build both pass; if the death-step test still passes on the patched build, STOP with 'control-mismatch: <numbers>'. THE BAD-ARGUMENT TEST AND THE CONTROLS ABOVE are the positive controls per mechanism.\nON THE BUILT TREE (origin/main; no P2 file exists): build, run both files with -q -s. They must be red for the stated reason: field_noise.h and economy_field_noise.c do not exist, so the cc build of library A fails (assert res.returncode == 0); paste that failing assertion line verbatim (file:line and the message head) for each of the two files, and the green line of test_ctrl_p1_stub_builds. If any case is red for another reason, fix the test and say so. Dump the premises from one real run of P1's pieces (the stub: kind, height at the origin, at (12000, 12000), water at the lake stub centre (8,000, 8,000); whether numpy is importable) and the 'Rule pins' lines your two files carry with the rule_pins_tests.py check output for them. Thresholds, windows and tolerances: none invented (every number from the spec, a named draft or a gap ruling; list each with its source in the report). Pre-gate: ${PREGATE('<worktree>', TEST_FILES)} (red tests make the test step REJECT by design: quote that line and say the other steps are OK; the pins step must be OK). Report ok, branch, sha, summary (the failing lines, the control line, the premises, the number list), red_ids.`, { label: 'tests:P2', phase: 'Tests', schema: REPORT, agentType: 'engineer', model: 'sonnet' })
const mkProto = () => (PROBE_OK && done('proto')) || agent(`${RULES}\nRole: probe measurer (test side, Engineer; the writer of the P2 tests is another agent), for the SPECIAL RULE of P2 of ${SPEC}. You write NO repo file and make NO branch: you work in a detached worktree of origin/main (P1 is on it; git worktree add --detach <path> origin/main, suffix vg-p2r-proto, removed after with git worktree remove, no --force) and write only into the scratch directory ${PROTO_DIR} (mkdir -p with that literal path). Purpose: the probe does not exist yet, so measure the SHAPE the spec's rule gives on the REAL C noise, before any Build. Write ${PROTO_DIR}/ref_probe.c, a scratch REFERENCE MODEL in C of the spec rule below, written from the spec text and this interface only (never from any growth_probe.c, never from ${FIN_REF}), compiled by cc -std=c11 -O2 -fno-fast-math -ffp-contract=off -I<worktree>/csrc ref_probe.c <worktree>/csrc/terrain_noise.c (the real om_tn_fbm2; the harness main reads lo and hi from argv so the same model can be re-run with a built library's pins), plus ${PROTO_DIR}/measure.py (pure Python: runs the model, computes the spectrum) and ${PROTO_DIR}/results.json. The model implements EVERYTHING in the interface below for the probe and for om_field_hop_cost (with lo and hi as inputs), no lanes, with the GAP 2, 12 and 13 rulings as given. Pins: measure the pin the way the P2 test will (gap 5 reading: the min and max of om_tn_fbm2(seed + 420, gx * 8192, gy * 8192, 3, 32768) over gx, gy in 0..99 for each of the seeds 1..64, one pair for the whole sweep) and use it at slack 0 (lo = the measured min, hi = the measured max) AND at slack 0.05 of the span on each side (lo = min - 0.05 * span, hi = max + 0.05 * span). Measure, side 240, one core at (120, 120), flat dry ground, for seeds 1..10: (a) the front: for steps 3, 5, 10 and 20 (core age = steps) the reached set (P > 0) radial profile in 32 sectors (sector = floor(atan2(dy, dx) / (2 pi / 32)) mod 32, the largest cell distance of any reached cell in it, empty = 0) and the harmonic 4 plus 8 share of its one-sided AC power spectrum (mean removed, DFT, harmonics 1 to 16; 0.0 for zero power); (b) the first ring: the eight compass-ray reaches after 10 steps and their spread; (c) the lots: for each core age in 10, 20, 30, 40, 100, 200 the lot count and the same profile and share of the lots (kind 'lots'; the front rows are kind 'front' with age = steps); (d) out_death_step for age 150 (one per seed, field death_steps; death_step = seed 1) and the east-ray distance of the last reached cell (the largest gx - 120 with P > 0 at gy = 120; field east_reach_max = its maximum over the seeds); (e) the cost shares pooled over seeds 1..64 on the pin sample (cost_share_min and cost_share_max over the three costs); (f) the lot count at ages 10 and 40 for seed 1; (g) the sanity controls: a clean square, a noisy square, an octagon, a diamond and a smooth blob lot set through the same share function (the spec says 0.99, 0.80, 0.997, 0.99 and 0.13 to 0.20; print yours). Each of (a) and (c) at slack 0 (field share) and slack 0.05 (field share_slack5). REPORT, NOT FIX: if any share is above ${SHAPE_HARM}, or any death step is outside 100 to 600, you change nothing (no rule, no pin, no parameter, no detector), you only report the numbers; do not explain them away. Fill the schema: probe = one row per (kind, age, seed) with share, share_slack5 and lots; death_steps; death_step; first_ring_min_spread (the smallest spread over the seeds); cost_share_min and cost_share_max; lots_age10; lots_age40; pin_lo and pin_hi (the slack 0 pins); summary = the worst share per kind and age, the death steps, the control values, and the exact command to re-run the model; model_src = the full source text of ref_probe.c followed by measure.py (it is attached to the stop report for the Architect). ok=true when the measurement ran (even if shares exceed ${SHAPE_HARM}); ok=false only when you could not run it (stop_reason).\n${IFACE}\n${RULED}`, { label: 'tests:P2-probe', phase: 'Tests', schema: REPORT, agentType: 'engineer', model: 'sonnet' })
const [tests, proto] = await parallel([mkTests, mkProto])
out = { ...out, tests, proto }
if (!(tests && tests.ok)) return { ...out, stopped: 'tests' }
if (!(proto && proto.ok)) return { ...out, stopped: 'proto' }
const over = (proto.probe || []).filter(p => p.share > SHAPE_HARM || (typeof p.share_slack5 === 'number' && p.share_slack5 > SHAPE_HARM))
const deathBad = (proto.death_steps || []).filter(d => d <= 100 || d >= 600)
const borderBad = typeof proto.east_reach_max === 'number' && proto.east_reach_max >= 119
if (borderBad) return { ...out, stopped: 'front-touches-border', east_reach_max: proto.east_reach_max, need: 'REPORT TO THE ARCHITECT, NOT FIX (GAP 4 ruling): the reference model gives an east-ray reach of ' + proto.east_reach_max + ' cells on the centred age-150 core (the ruling asks for under 119, so the field never touches the border). No Build starts.' }
if (deathBad.length) return { ...out, stopped: 'death-step-outside', death_steps: proto.death_steps, need: 'REPORT TO THE ARCHITECT, NOT FIX (spec :136: a measured out_death_step outside 100 and 600 is reported before anything is changed): the reference model gives death steps ' + JSON.stringify(proto.death_steps) + '. No Build starts; the Architect rules the bounds or the rule (Westley owns the thresholds).' }
if (!PROBE_OK) { // Architect 2026-10-14: the shape table goes to him before Build ALWAYS, not only when a share is above the pin; over may be empty
  return { ...out, stopped: 'harmonic-share', pin: SHAPE_HARM, over, probe: proto.probe, death_steps: proto.death_steps, first_ring_min_spread: proto.first_ring_min_spread, cost_share_min: proto.cost_share_min, cost_share_max: proto.cost_share_max, lots_age10: proto.lots_age10, lots_age40: proto.lots_age40, pin_lo: proto.pin_lo, pin_hi: proto.pin_hi, model_src: proto.model_src, need: 'REPORT TO THE ARCHITECT, NOT FIX: per-seed 4th+8th harmonic shares of the front (kind front: 3, 5, 10, 20 steps) and of the lots (kind lots: ages 10 to 200) beside the pin, the first-ring spread, the cost shares, the death steps and the lot counts (the probe measurer\'s reference model on the real C noise; table in probe, rows above the pin in over). No Build starts. Resume with args.probeOk = the Architect\'s go text, args.skip = { tests: \'' + tests.branch + '\', proto: \'x\' }. VG-P3 launches only after this report reaches the Architect and he says so.' }
}

phase('Build')
const BCOMMON = (u) => `${RULES}\nRole: Doer (rules.md section (a)) for P2 of ${SPEC}, unit ${u}. Build units are small: about one file and about 100 lines; stop and report if yours needs far more. Tests were written first by a different agent (the unit's branch line below merges them); never edit a test.\n${IFACE}\n${RULED}${PROBE_RULED}\nSTARTING FILES: the rev 4a files of ${FIN_REF} (spec :136: the builder starts from push/vg-p2-fin). Do NOT merge that branch (it conflicts and carries the old tests and a ledger row); take a file with git checkout ${FIN_REF} -- <path> and stage it by name. The old names ${OLD_NOISE} and ${OLD_H} must not exist on your branch when you push (git mv them to the new names, see your unit).\nGeneral: every numeric literal carries a comment naming its source (spec rev 6 line, DRAFT-<name>, or economy_density.c:<line>); no libm call beyond sqrt fabs floor round fmin fmax; no static mutable state; comments name R-193-01 or R-193-09 where the code serves it and a See also: line between the probe and economy_density.c (the probe is the copy P3 must match); no comment or name that still says lot order or lot noise. Report ok, branch, sha, summary (the test lines with PASS or FAIL, the numeric literals you added or changed with the source of each), red_ids, parked.`
const mkB1 = (extra) => done('b1') || agent(`${BCOMMON('B1 field noise and lanes')}\nBranch push/vg-p2r-b1, suffix vg-p2r-b1, from origin/main; merge origin/${tests.branch}${rulingMerge()}${extra}. Files: ${H_NOISE} and ${N_NOISE} ONLY. Start with git checkout ${FIN_REF} -- ${OLD_NOISE} ${OLD_H}, then git mv ${OLD_H} ${H_NOISE} and git mv ${OLD_NOISE} ${N_NOISE} (do NOT bring ${C_PROBE}: it is unit B2's, and without it the library builds). ${H_NOISE}: the header exactly as the INTERFACE gives it (guard OM_FIELD_NOISE_H, includes layout_internal.h and <stdint.h>; om_field_hop_cost, om_field_noise_range, om_lane_build). ${N_NOISE}: delete om_lot_noise_q16, the 0.7..1.4 band and every lot-noise comment; add om_field_hop_cost, om_field_noise_range and om_field_apply_cost as the INTERFACE says (the helper declared in field_noise.h and defined in this file) (the retired om_lot_noise_range becomes om_field_noise_range, same pin mechanism); om_lane_build stays as it is in the starting file (diff its body against ${FIN_REF}: only its include and comment names may differ; say so in the report). Pin lo and hi from the numbers the noise test prints ('NOISE_RANGE measured_min=... measured_max=...'): run the group first with the pins as placeholders, read the printed measured extremes, then set the two constants within DRAFT-noise-range-slack of them (lo at or below the measured min and no more than 0.05 of the span below it, hi likewise) and comment 'DRAFT-field-noise-range, measured by ${T_LANES} over seeds 1 to 64 (gap 5 reading)'; put pin_lo and pin_hi in the report. Done when: make OPT=-O2 WERROR=1 libouroboros.so libouroboros_dbg.so builds with no warning, the three lints of your rules are clean, and pytest ${T_LANES} passes in full (every noise and lane case and the lane controls). Pre-gate: ${PREGATE('<worktree>', T_LANES)}. `, { label: 'build:P2-B1', phase: 'Build', schema: REPORT, agentType: 'doer', model: 'sonnet' })
const mkB2 = (b1, extra) => done('build') || agent(`${BCOMMON('B2 growth probe')}\nBranch push/vg-p2r, suffix vg-p2r, from origin/main; merge origin/${tests.branch} and origin/${b1.branch}${rulingMerge()}${extra}. File: ${C_PROBE} ONLY. Start with git checkout ${FIN_REF} -- ${C_PROBE} (216 lines). Change it to the INTERFACE: (1) include field_noise.h in place of lot_noise.h; (2) the one line '#define PROBE_HOP_COST(seed, gx, gy) om_field_hop_cost((seed), (gx), (gy))', the only place a hop cost is taken, filled once per run into a local uint8 cost grid; (3) the hop: v = om_field_apply_cost(P[i], f, cost[j]) (the GAP 12 helper from field_noise.h; no inline copy of the multiplications), the gate floor_mod(s, cost[j]) == 0 with s = floor_div(tick, 60) = k - max_age (GAP 13 ruling; the rev 4a file already steps at the virtual tick (k - max_age) * 60; floor_mod written by hand for a negative s), the accept test and the Q16 truncation unchanged; (4) the lot step: delete the lot key and the om_lot_noise_q16 call; the candidates of the 97 x 97 scan square (core_of == c, density >= THRESHOLD_1, no lot) taken in DESCENDING density, ties by lower cell index, by the hand-written merge sort the rev 4a file already has (reuse it with the new compare: scan_less, scan_sort) and a lot created on each until the core stands quota_c lots; (5) keep the tenth parameter lot_cap and PROBE_LOT_CAP 8192 exactly as the starting file has them (GAP 2 ruling); the file still does not include om_internal.h; (6) rewrite the header comment of the file (it says the lot order carries the noise: it is the field now, R-193-01) and every comment that names the lot order. Keep the probe's lane-free loop, the pre-growth schedule, the per-core maturity and economy, PROBE_BASE_DECAY and PROBE_NONWATER_FAR each on its own line. Done when: make OPT=-O2 WERROR=1 libouroboros.so libouroboros_dbg.so builds with no warning, the three lints are clean, BOTH ${T_LANES} and ${T_PROBE} pass in full (run with -q -s), and ${PREGATE('<worktree>', TEST_FILES)} ends PRE_GATE verdict OK. grep -rn "lot_noise\\|om_lot_noise" csrc tests must find nothing. HARMONIC SHARE (SPECIAL RULE): the tests print 'FIELD_FRONT' and 'PROBE_SHAPE' lines; copy every one into the report field probe (kind front or lots, age, seed, share, lots) and the death steps, the first-ring spreads, the cost shares, the lot counts at ages 10 and 40 and the pins into their fields. If ANY share is above ${SHAPE_HARM}: the shape test is red for a real reason, not a defect: you change NOTHING (no test, no pin, no rule), push the branch as it stands, and stop with stop_reason 'harmonic-share: <the rows above the pin>'; do not iterate. A red from the same cause is the only red you may leave. A death step outside 100 to 600: the same, stop_reason 'death-step-outside: <numbers>'; an east-ray reach of 119 cells or more on the centred age-150 core: the same, stop_reason 'front-touches-border: <numbers>' (GAP 4 ruling). `, { label: 'build:P2-B2', phase: 'Build', schema: REPORT, agentType: 'doer', model: 'sonnet' })
const b1 = await withRuling((x) => mkB1(x))
out = { ...out, b1 }
if (!(b1 && b1.ok)) return { ...out, stopped: 'build' }
const build = await withRuling((x) => mkB2(b1, x))
out = { ...out, build }
const builtOver = ((build && build.probe) || []).filter(p => p.share > SHAPE_HARM)
if (builtOver.length || /^harmonic-share/.test((build && build.stop_reason) || '')) {
  return { ...out, stopped: 'harmonic-share-built', pin: SHAPE_HARM, over: builtOver, probe: build.probe, death_steps: build.death_steps, lots_age10: build.lots_age10, lots_age40: build.lots_age40, need: 'REPORT TO THE ARCHITECT, NOT FIX: the BUILT probe (real growth_probe.c on the real C noise) has a share above the pin; the branch ' + (build && build.branch) + ' is pushed as is; no Check, no landing. VG-P3 launches only after this report reaches the Architect and he says so.' }
}
if (/^(death-step-outside|front-touches-border)/.test((build && build.stop_reason) || '')) return { ...out, stopped: 'death-step-outside-built', need: 'REPORT TO THE ARCHITECT, NOT FIX: ' + build.stop_reason + '; the branch ' + build.branch + ' is pushed as is; no Check, no landing.' }
if (!(build && build.ok)) return { ...out, stopped: 'build' }

phase('Check')
const checks = await parallel([
  () => agent(`${RO}\nRole: gate checker (Engineer), rules.md section (c), read-only, detached worktree at origin/${build.branch} (suffix chk-vg-p2r; remove it after with git worktree remove, no --force). Spec: ${SPEC}.\n${IFACE}\n${RULED}${PROBE_RULED}\n(1) FOOTPRINT: the diff versus origin/main touches only ${FILES} and ${TEST_FILES}; no existing file edited; ${OLD_NOISE} and ${OLD_H} do not exist; no change in csrc/om_internal.h, csrc/ouroboros_sim.h, signatures.toml, test_signatures_internal.py, reach_allowlist.toml, symbol_modules.toml, the Makefile, csrc/terrain_noise.c, csrc/layout_*; no .uid or .import noise; grep -rn "lot_noise" csrc tests finds nothing. (2a) HELPER (GAP 12): om_field_apply_cost is declared in field_noise.h, defined once in ${N_NOISE} as ((v * f) * f) * f with cost multiplications left to right, and growth_probe.c calls it for every hop (no inline multiplication by the factor cost times, no pow); the east-ray reach on the centred age-150 core is under 119 for seeds 1..10 (quote the PROBE_DEATH lines). (2) NUMBERS: every numeric literal in the three C files listed with its source (spec rev 6 line, DRAFT name, economy_density.c or economy_lots.c line, or a gap ruling); blocking true for a number with no source; PROBE_BASE_DECAY and PROBE_NONWATER_FAR each defined once on its own line; PROBE_HOP_COST defined once on one line and the only place the probe takes a cost; the pins lo and hi lie within the slack of the measured extremes (read the test output); the cost buckets 21845 and 43691 as spec :132. (2b) om_lane_build: diff its body against ${FIN_REF}:${OLD_NOISE} and quote the diff: only include and comment names may differ (spec :133 'kept as is'); any other difference is blocking. (2c) MESSAGES: every assertion in the two test files that proves R-193-01 carries the sentence '${R193}' in its message; list the assertions and quote one; each test file carries its own 'Rule pins:' line naming every R-id it mentions: run ~/Projects/ouroboros-manifold/.venv/bin/python scripts/specfactory/rule_pins_tests.py check <worktree> --only ${TEST_FILES.split(', ').join(' ')} and quote it; blocking on a missing message or a PINS REJECT. (3) LINTS: make OPT=-O2 WERROR=1 libouroboros.so libouroboros_dbg.so clean; scripts/specfactory/libm_lint.py csrc, scripts/specfactory/alg_constants.py --lint csrc and with --strict, scripts/specfactory/reach_lint.py (read how merge_gate.sh calls it) and the size lint: quote each last line; confirm by reading that no qsort, bsearch, pow or other banned call is used and the sort is hand-written. (4) TESTS: run ${T_LANES} and ${T_PROBE} in full with -q -s under timeout 1800 and paste the PASS/FAIL line of each and every PROBE_SHAPE, FIELD_FRONT, FIELD_FIRST_RING, FIELD_COST_SHARE, NOISE_RANGE, PROBE_DEATH, PROBE_LOTS and PROBE_DIFFER line; the worst share per age and per kind; the death steps. (5) REVERT CHECK: in the detached worktree only, remove ${N_NOISE} and ${H_NOISE} (run the tests against a scratch copy of the tree where the two files are absent; never modify the checked-out files of origin/${build.branch} itself) and confirm both test files go red at the cc build assertion; then restore the files in the scratch copy only and confirm green; separately, in a scratch copy, force every cost to 1 (the PROBE_HOP_COST line) and replace the divergence constants by 1.01 yourself, and confirm the noise-off and divergence controls behave as the report said. Never use git stash or git checkout of the checked-out tree. (6) DETERMINISM: run the same-input byte-equality cases and one extra -O0 versus -O2 comparison of om_growth_probe_run output for seeds 1 and 2, age 40, quote the digests. (7) Pre-gate on this tree, every line verbatim: ${PREGATE('<this worktree>', TEST_FILES)}; list each WARN (expected: provenance WARN no spec key for VG-P2) and any footprint line naming an unowned file (blocking). (8) Report what you did not run. Report pass, blocking, evidence (every PASS/FAIL line, the literal list, the digests).`, { label: 'check:P2', phase: 'Check', schema: VERDICT, agentType: 'engineer', model: 'sonnet' }),
  () => agent(`${RO}\nRole: model cross-checker (Engineer), rules.md section (c), read-only on the repo: detached worktree at origin/${build.branch} (suffix chk-vg-p2r-model; remove after, no --force); you may write only inside ${PROTO_DIR}. The probe measurer left a scratch reference model of the spec rule there (${PROTO_DIR}/ref_probe.c, measure.py, results.json; written from the spec before the build). Compare the BUILT probe (csrc/growth_probe.c, compiled with csrc/terrain_noise.c and csrc/economy_field_noise.c and P1's stub as the P2 tests do, driven by ctypes) against the model, fed the built library's own pins (om_field_noise_range lo and hi) so the two use the same costs: for seeds 1 to 3 and the cases (a) one core at (120, 120), ages 10, 40 and 100; (b) two cores at (80, 80) and (150, 150) with ages 10 and 40; (c) six cores spread over the grid with ages 5, 10, 20, 30, 40, 40 (cells you choose, at least 60 cells apart); on side 240: byte-compare out_P, out_density and out_lot_core and compare the lot counts and out_death_step. Equal everywhere: pass. Any difference: it is a SPEC-INTERPRETATION difference between two implementations written from the same text: pass false, blocking false, and the evidence lists the first differing cell, the case, both values and the spec sentence each implementation followed (so the Architect rules it; nothing is fixed here). Also re-run the model's shape table (fronts and lots) with the built pins and say whether any share is above ${SHAPE_HARM}. Report pass, blocking, evidence.`, { label: 'check:P2-model', phase: 'Check', schema: VERDICT, agentType: 'engineer', model: 'sonnet' }),
])
out = { ...out, checks }
if (!(checks[0] && checks[0].pass)) return { ...out, stopped: 'check' }
if (!(checks[1] && checks[1].pass)) return { ...out, stopped: 'check-model', need: 'the built probe and the scratch reference model differ: a spec-interpretation difference for the Architect (see checks[1].evidence); nothing landed' }

phase('Clerk')
const clerk = await agent(`${RULES}\nRole: landing clerk (Engineer), rules.md section (b). ${PUSH_MAIN ? 'The push to main at the end IS authorised on a clean gate (Westley\'s standing word for clean-gate pushes, passed by the Dispatcher), subject to the known-red rule below.' : 'Do NOT push to main (args.pushMain false): branch only.'} First: git fetch origin; confirm P1 is still on origin/main (git ls-tree origin/main csrc/layout_internal.h csrc/layout_terrain.c csrc/layout_engine.c tests/csim/layout_stub_terrain.c all present; VG-P1 attached); if not, stop with stop_reason "p1-not-landed" and push nothing. Branch push/vg-p2r-land, suffix vg-p2r-land, from origin/main; merge origin/${tests.branch}, origin/${build.branch}${rulingMerge()} (the build branch already contains the unit branch; say if a merge needed more than a clean merge). Stage files by name only: never git commit -a, never git add -A, never a *.import or *.uid file. Build (make OPT=-O2 WERROR=1 libouroboros.so libouroboros_dbg.so and, to leave the tree as the gate expects, make pipe/ouroboros_pipe pipe/ouroboros_pipe_dbg); run ${T_LANES} and ${T_PROBE} (PASS/FAIL per file; the merge gate cannot run acceptance files for a comma list of pieces: the acceptance-ids, acceptance-verdict and undertest steps WARN and are quoted). Pre-gate before the lock (section (b)): ${PREGATE('<landing worktree>', TEST_FILES)}; it must end OK. Full gate, EXACTLY section (b), detached, from the landing worktree: mkdir -p ~/Projects/om-push/tmp-vg-p2r; flock -w 14400 ~/Projects/om-push/gate.lock env TMPDIR=~/Projects/om-push/tmp-vg-p2r MERGE_GATE_SUITE_TIMEOUT=2400 MERGE_GATE_PLAYTHROUGH_TIMEOUT=2400 MERGE_GATE_PLAY_TIMEOUT=900 MERGE_GATE_PIECES=<landing worktree>/docs/northstar/plans/push/pieces.toml scripts/specfactory/merge_gate.sh <landing worktree> origin/main ${PIECES} >~/Projects/om-push/tmp-vg-p2r/gate.log 2>&1 (three positional arguments; the last is ONE comma list with no spaces; add any further owner id a footprint line names, and re-run the pre-gate); poll gate.log for the ^GATE look line, one foreground command under 10 minutes at a time (poll no more often than every 3 to 5 minutes), then pgrep -f '^bash scripts/specfactory/merge_gate.sh' to confirm no gate for the worktree still runs (never pgrep your own command line); the verdict is the set of GATE <stage> REJECT lines. Flake rule per section (b). Delete only the merge_gate_before_* directories under your own TMPDIR. KNOWN-RED RULE (section (b), Architect 2026-10-12): push main only when EVERY GATE REJECT line names a test or play listed by exact id in scripts/specfactory/lane_plays_known_red.txt or scripts/specfactory/gd_tests_known_red.txt on the landing tree (both exist on origin/main; at c6f3f883 the GD file lists tests/test_vg_e_e1p.gd and the plays file three plays); a reject outside those files means branch only, every REJECT line quoted, never a push. P2 touches no Godot code, so the GD known-red tests are not this piece's: list them by name if they reject and do not fix them. If no REJECT, or only listed ones: in pieces.toml flip VG-P2 to status = { state = "attached", attach_sha = "<landing sha7>" } (the format of the attached rows) and set tests_pending = false, and rewrite that row's leading comment (pieces.toml:2342, which still says rev 4a and lot-order noise: now places lane spec rev 6, field noise as a hop cost, contour/water/fallback lanes and the C growth probe, all new files, P3 wires them), its depends_on comment and its size_estimate to the rev 6 facts (the comment says P2 links csrc/layout_terrain.c: it does not, GAP 1; the size_estimate names lot_noise.h, economy_lot_noise.c, om_lot_noise_q16 and DRAFT-lot-noise-*: now field_noise.h with three prototypes, economy_field_noise.c with om_field_hop_cost, om_field_noise_range and om_lane_build, growth_probe.c with om_growth_probe_run, two pytest files, DRAFT-field-*, DRAFT-lane-*, DRAFT-shape-harm 0.5); in docs/northstar/plans/2026-10-07-visible-game-programme.md edit the lane row for lane P ONLY if it already exists (On main "P2 at <sha7>: field noise, contour lanes and the growth probe landed; the shape report is in the landing report; P3 waits for the Architect"), otherwise write nothing there and list "no lane P row" in the report; write nothing about status anywhere else (no ROADMAP lane row, no journal line); there is NO look stage and NO shot for this piece (sim code, nothing the player sees; say so). Commit all of that in the landing commit (normal prose, Co-Authored-By trailer). Right before the push: git fetch origin; if origin/main moved, merge it in (say so; ledger and queue appends keep both sides) and re-run the pre-gate; push the branch, then ${PUSH_MAIN ? 'git push origin HEAD:main (only under the known-red rule above)' : 'stop at the branch (args.pushMain false)'}. Write .wt-done (date, branch, pushed sha) after the push and remove the worktree only if it is clean and its HEAD is contained in origin (git branch -r --contains HEAD), else leave it with .wt-done. The report's summary carries: the stage lines verbatim ("OK per stage" or every GATE REJECT line), the WARN lines, the two test-file lines, main head, and the plain statement "P2: the field noise (hop cost), the contour/water/fallback lanes and the growth probe are built, tested and linked into the library but called from no game path (P3 wires them); no player-visible change; the shape report for the Architect (per-seed 4th+8th harmonic share of the front and of the lots beside the 0.5 pin, the first-ring spread, the cost shares, the death steps, the lot counts at ages 10 and 40) is: " followed by the FIELD_FRONT, FIELD_FIRST_RING, FIELD_COST_SHARE, PROBE_SHAPE, PROBE_DEATH and PROBE_LOTS lines of the landing run (all of them). Report ok, branch, sha, summary, red_ids, probe (the rows), death_steps, first_ring_min_spread, cost_share_min, cost_share_max, lots_age10, lots_age40.`, { label: 'clerk:P2', phase: 'Clerk', schema: REPORT, agentType: 'engineer', model: 'sonnet' })
